## Final SOC Summary

A suspicious URL obtained from a phishing email was investigated through DNS analysis, reverse DNS lookup, URLScan analysis, and redirect examination. The investigation identified the associated infrastructure and observed redirect behavior commonly used in phishing campaigns. Although no direct malicious classification was available, the URL should be treated cautiously due to its phishing context and further monitored for related malicious activity.

## Lessons Learned

This lab improved practical phishing investigation skills by demonstrating how SOC analysts analyze suspicious URLs, enrich indicators, identify infrastructure relationships, and document findings using evidence-based reporting.
